<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iziaslav II of Kiev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1097–<a href="/years/1154">1154</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Iziaslav Mstislavich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iziaslav II Mstislavich, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-ii-monomakh">Vladimir Monomakh</a>, was Grand Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> at intervals from 1146 until his death. His reign was dominated by a bitter struggle for Kiev with his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-dolgoruky">Yuri Dolgoruky</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a>. His descendants held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a> as a hereditary domain and later founded the Kingdom of Galicia-Volhynia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iziaslav-ii-of-kiev.jpg" alt="Iziaslav II of Kiev" width="320" height="664" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Izyaslav_II_-_fresco_of_the_Novospassky_Monastery.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
